{
	"about": "Standard formatter conformance table (D174). Each case pipes `input` through `name` with `args` and expects `expect`. Both hosts run it: PuzzleKit from tests/formatters.test.js, Sites from its Go formatter tests. JSON null is the missing value, as input and as expected output. A case with `zone` renders in that IANA time zone; every other case is zone-independent. Only locale-independent behavior belongs here: the locale-rendered formatters appear only through their iso presets, pluralize's word choice (small counts), and number_with_delimiter with an explicit delimiter. The raw rows pin the shared markup allowlist (D174): rich text that survives, then an XSS corpus in which every case must come out inert. A raw row's expect is the exact sanitized markup; newline_to_br's is the escaped text with a <br> per line break. The `t` rows (D175) add a `locale`: the key is looked up in `translations[locale]`, then in `translations.en` (the default locale); each host fills and loads the tables its own way (PuzzleKit fills at build time, Sites falls back at lookup). `{count}` rows stay in `en`. An exact count of 0 uses an entry's `zero` form when it has one, in every locale (D175).",
	"translations": {
		"en": { "cart.title": "Your cart", "nav.home": "Home", "greeting": "Hello, {name}!", "echo": "{a} and {b}", "item_count": { "one": "{count} item", "other": "{count} items" }, "cart_items": { "zero": "Your cart is empty", "one": "{count} item", "other": "{count} items" } },
		"pl": { "cart.title": "Twój koszyk", "files": { "one": "{count} plik", "few": "{count} pliki", "many": "{count} plików", "other": "{count} pliku" }, "pages": { "one": "{count} strona", "other": "{count} stron" } }
	},
